{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/best-before-or-use-by/audio/main-c2e2575cdb3a.mp3","durationSec":129.624,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.94,"text":"A use-by date is about food safety."},{"start":2.5,"end":6.04,"text":"Do not eat food after this date, even if it looks and smells fine."},{"start":6.94,"end":10.24,"text":"Food can contain harmful bacteria that you cannot see or smell."},{"start":10.86,"end":16.68,"text":"In the UK, meat products and ready-to-eat salads are two examples of foods that can have a use-by date."},{"start":16.68,"end":19.62,"text":"You can eat them until midnight on the date if you stored them correctly."},{"start":20.32,"end":23.56,"text":"You can also cook or freeze the food on or before that date."},{"start":24.04,"end":26.86,"text":"After the date, do not eat, cook, or freeze it."},{"start":28.42,"end":31.8,"text":"A best-before date is about quality, not safety."},{"start":32.32,"end":36.72,"text":"It tells you when food may start to lose its best taste, texture, or colour."},{"start":36.72,"end":41.44,"text":"Frozen peas and dried pasta are two examples of foods that often have a best-before date."},{"start":42.06,"end":46.42,"text":"After the date, the food is usually safe to eat, but its quality may be lower."},{"start":47.18,"end":51.82,"text":"For a best-before food, you can use sight, smell, or taste to help decide."},{"start":51.82,"end":57.1,"text":"For example, check bread for mould, or taste a crisp to see if it is stale."},{"start":57.96,"end":60.58,"text":"Also check that you stored the food as the packet says."},{"start":61.48,"end":64.8,"text":"The dates work as expected only when you store the food correctly."},{"start":65.62,"end":70.56,"text":"The packet may say “keep refrigerated” or “store in a cool, dry place.”"},{"start":71.56,"end":74.2,"text":"It may also tell you what to do after you open it."},{"start":74.92,"end":80.64,"text":"For example, a chilled food can become unsafe before its use-by date if you leave it out of the fridge."},{"start":81.22,"end":84.26,"text":"Dried food can lose quality early if it gets wet."},{"start":85.4,"end":88.28,"text":"Read the storage instructions every time, and follow them."},{"start":89.46,"end":94.38,"text":"If you cannot eat food before its use-by date, you may be able to cook or freeze it in time."},{"start":95.46,"end":98.78,"text":"You can freeze food on or before the use-by date."},{"start":98.78,"end":104.16,"text":"Keep the freezer at −18°C and follow the packet’s freezing and defrosting instructions."},{"start":104.7,"end":108.22,"text":"After you defrost the food, use it within 24 hours."},{"start":108.88,"end":111.68,"text":"You can also cook food on or before the date."},{"start":112.38,"end":118.4,"text":"Cool it, keep it in the fridge, and eat it within 48 hours, or freeze it."},{"start":119.24,"end":129.04,"text":"For example, if raw chicken has a use-by date of Tuesday and you cannot cook it by then, freeze it on Monday or Tuesday—not Wednesday."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.16},{"text":"use-by","start":0.16,"end":0.48},{"text":"date","start":0.48,"end":0.8},{"text":"is","start":0.8,"end":1.02},{"text":"about","start":1.02,"end":1.26},{"text":"food","start":1.26,"end":1.52},{"text":"safety","start":1.52,"end":1.94},{"text":"Do","start":2.5,"end":2.58},{"text":"not","start":2.58,"end":2.82},{"text":"eat","start":2.82,"end":3.04},{"text":"food","start":3.04,"end":3.32},{"text":"after","start":3.32,"end":3.6},{"text":"this","start":3.6,"end":3.86},{"text":"date","start":3.86,"end":4.1},{"text":"even","start":4.32,"end":4.48},{"text":"if","start":4.48,"end":4.64},{"text":"it","start":4.64,"end":4.74},{"text":"looks","start":4.74,"end":5},{"text":"and","start":5,"end":5.3},{"text":"smells","start":5.3,"end":5.6},{"text":"fine","start":5.6,"end":6.04},{"text":"Food","start":6.94,"end":7.06},{"text":"can","start":7.06,"end":7.26},{"text":"contain","start":7.26,"end":7.64},{"t